{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I guard it.</b> Concerning the Shekhinah, which is in Zion." "<b>At every moment I water it.</b> A parable for prophecy, that it shall not cease." "<b>Lest anyone visit upon it.</b> Rabbi Jonah the grammarian said that פן is like לא, and the yud of יפקוד is in place of the alef as the sign of the speaker, like אָרְחֵי חַיִּים פֶּן תִפַּלְס (Proverbs 5:6). The meaning is: upon all the nations I visit — not upon her. And Rabbi Isaac ben Saul, may his memory be for a blessing, said that יפקד is like לא נפקד ממנו איש (Numbers 31:49); it connects with לרגעים אשקנה פן יבול עליה — each one of them, lest he wither upon her, like נובלת עליה (Isaiah 1:30). And Rabbi Moses the Cohen said: פן יפקד עליה — the enemy. I guard it night and day. And this is straight in my eyes."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {2 "Resolved נ\"ע as 'may his memory be for a blessing' (נוח נפשו / נשמתו עדן)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:24.895086237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}